/*
  Testing & Data Quality Framework
To ensure the high reliability and integrity of the data migrating from the Bronze Layer (Raw) to the Silver Layer (Cleaned & Standardized), a comprehensive Data Quality Audit was conducted across all datasets.

Key Testing Areas & Validations:

Primary & Foreign Key Integrity: Verified uniqueness and nullability of primary keys (appointment_id, bill_id, doctor_id, patient_id, treatment_id) and validated referential integrity across relational entities.

String Cleaning & Standardization: Checked for unwanted leading/trailing whitespace using TRIM() checks and ensured consistent casing for critical text fields (e.g., standardizing gender to Male/Female and lowercasing email addresses).

Data Types & Precision Adjustments: Handled time-precision formats by casting appointment_time to TIME(0) to truncate unnecessary fractional seconds.

Domain & Business Logic Rules: Validated that dates (date_of_birth, registration_date, treatment_date) do not exceed current dates, verified that positive values are maintained for financial amounts and costs (amount > 0), and confirmed phone number and insurance string formats.

Result: All validation checks passed successfully. Data loaded into the Silver Layer is fully cleansed, standardized, and primed for Dimensional Modeling in the Gold Layer.
*/

---------------------appointments--------------

--check unwanted spaces
select  appointment_id
from bronze.appointments
where appointment_id != TRIM(appointment_id)

--check redundancy
select appointment_id,count(*)
from bronze.appointments
group by appointment_id
having count(*)>1

--check nulls
select  appointment_id
from bronze.appointments
where appointment_id is null

--patient_id---
--check unwanted spaces
select  patient_id
from bronze.appointments
where patient_id not in (select distinct patient_id from bronze.patients)

--check nulls
select  patient_id
from bronze.appointments
where patient_id is null

--doctor_id--
--check unwanted spaces
select  doctor_id
from bronze.appointments
where TRIM(doctor_id) not in (select distinct doctor_id from bronze.doctors)

--check nulls
select  doctor_id
from bronze.appointments
where doctor_id is null

--appointment_date
--check null
select appointment_date
from bronze.appointments
where appointment_date is null

--appointment_time--
--check unwanted spaces
select appointment_time
from bronze.appointments
where CAST(appointment_time AS VARCHAR(20)) != TRIM(CAST(appointment_time AS VARCHAR(20)));

--edit format
SELECT CAST(appointment_time AS TIME(0)) AS appointment_time
FROM bronze.appointments;

--reason for visit-----
--Data Standardization & Consistency
select distinct reason_for_visit
from bronze.appointments
--unwanted spaces
select reason_for_visit
from bronze.appointments
where reason_for_visit != TRIM(reason_for_visit)

--status
--Data Standardization & Consistency
select distinct status
from bronze.appointments
--unwanted spaces
select status
from bronze.appointments
where status != TRIM(status)

